<%#
  The sign-in layout, copied from spree_admin 5.6.1 with one line changed.

  The client asked for his own picture on the admin sign-in screen, a different
  one per shop. The gem hardcodes `asset_path('login_sidebar_background.png')`,
  and that resolves to a digested file baked into the image at build time. Every
  shop here runs the SAME image, so there is no way to bake six different
  pictures in: the asset pipeline gives all six the one file.

  So the path comes from the environment instead, and each shop mounts its own
  picture at /rails/public/brand. Unset, it falls back to the gem's own asset and
  the screen looks exactly as it does today, which is what a shop with no picture
  supplied should get.

  Overridden rather than decorated because this is a view: Rails resolves the
  application's copy ahead of the engine's, and there is no hook in the middle of
  a layout to reach for instead.
%>
<% login_image = ENV["ADMIN_LOGIN_IMAGE"].presence || asset_path("login_sidebar_background.png") %>
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="<%= I18n.locale %>" dir="<%= html_dir %>">
  <head>
    <%= render "spree/admin/shared/head" %>
  </head>
  <body class="admin min-h-screen <%= controller_name %> <%= action_name %>" data-controller="dialog">
    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 lg:grid-cols-2 min-h-screen">
      <div
        class="hidden lg:block bg-gray-25 bg-cover bg-center bg-no-repeat"
        style="background-image: url('<%= login_image %>');"
      >
      </div>
      <div class="flex flex-col justify-center items-center p-6 lg:p-12">
        <div class="w-full max-w-md">
          <%= yield %>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <%= render "spree/admin/shared/dialog" %>
    <%= render "spree/admin/shared/alerts" %>
    <%= render "spree/admin/shared/turbo_confirm_dialog" %>
  </body>
</html>
